// The checker rejections this tree introduced after its pinned oracle was cut,
// gated the way _tests_/cases gates an `// error` case — a byte-for-byte
// comparison of `bit check`'s rendered stderr against a pinned `.expected` — but
// driven from a directory the corpus differential does not sweep. Wave 3's four
// came first; #2273 and #2236's three joined them, and #2428's one, all for the
// identical reason.
//
// The corpus, in _tests_/bit/checkercases/:
//   check_compare_type_mismatch.bit        E0053, #2232/#2123
//   check_not_comparable.bit               E0052/E0053, #2123
//   check_struct_literal_unknown_field.bit E0057, #2230
//   check_error_iface_satisfaction.bit     E0041, #2237
//   check_unicode_escape_range.bit         E0005, #2273
//   check_main_params.bit                  E0085, #2236
//   check_main_signature.bit               E0085 x2, #2236
//   check_main_result_float.bit            E0085, #2236
//   check_switch_case_label_type.bit       E0053, #2428
//   check_assert_enum_target.bit           E0041, #2104
//   check_let_binding_needs_type.bit       E0086 x2, #2147
//   check_string_index_assign.bit          E0087 x3, #2740
//   check_forof_map_single.bit             E0088, #2108
//   check_method_arg_concrete.bit          E0041, #2755
//   check_method_arg_iface.bit             E0041, #2755
//   check_method_arg_toomany.bit           E0050, #2755
//   check_method_arg_toofew.bit            E0050, #2755
//   check_func_field_arg_type.bit          E0041, #2786
//   check_func_field_arg_type_rev.bit      E0041, #2786
//   check_func_field_arg_arity.bit         E0050, #2786
//   check_namespace_import_unexported.bit  E0046, #2804
//   check_function_keyword_removed.bit     E0089, #2773
//   check_keyword_as_field.bit             E0021, #2248
//   check_keyword_as_param.bit             E0021, #2248
//   check_keyword_as_var.bit               E0021, #2248
//   check_forof_string.bit                 E0090 x2, #2013
//   check_forin_unsupported.bit            E0091 x2, #2162
//   check_forin_binder_type.bit            E0041, #2162
//   check_member_bad_token.bit             E0021, #2845
//   check_method_enum_receiver.bit         E0095, #2736
//   check_method_enum_alias_receiver.bit   E0095, #2738
//   check_invisible_nul_string.bit         E0097, #2165
//   check_invisible_bidi_unpaired_comment.bit E0097, #2165
//   check_invisible_zero_width_space.bit   E0097, #2165
//   check_invisible_feff_string.bit        E0097, #2989
//   check_catch_tail_type.bit              E0041, #2981
//   check_qualified_type_unknown.bit       E0046, #2118
//   check_qualified_type_unexported.bit    E0046, #2118
//   check_string_concat_hint.bit           E0053, #3010
//   check_builtin_call_arity.bit           E0050, #2998
//   check_arrow_method_param_shadow.bit    E0057, #3029
//   check_select_binder_narrow.bit         E0041, #3038
//   check_call_arg_iface_satisfy.bit       E0041, #3050
//   check_method_call_arg_iface_satisfy.bit E0041, #3050
//   check_match_arity_toofew.bit           E0050, #3060
//   check_match_arity_toomany.bit          E0050, #3060
//   check_assign_iface_satisfy.bit         E0041, #3061
//   check_send_iface_satisfy.bit           E0041, #3061
//   check_composite_field_iface_satisfy.bit E0041, #3061
//   check_composite_map_iface_satisfy.bit  E0041, #3061
//   check_composite_slice_iface_satisfy.bit E0041, #3061
//   check_userconv_iface_satisfy.bit       E0041, #3064
//   check_chan_len.bit                     E0099 x2, #2021
//   check_match_wildcard_not_last.bit      E0100, #2294
//   check_match_wildcard_unreachable.bit   E0101, #2294
//   check_unknown_member_literal.bit       E0057 x3, #3444
//   check_unknown_member_binary_const.bit  E0057, #3449
//   check_class_reserved_spelling.bit      E0021, #3446
//   check_shadowed_conversion_note.bit     E0041 + note, #3474
//   check_catch_exit_shadowed.bit          E0041, #3471
//   check_invisible_identifier_binding.bit E0097, #3465
//   check_time_since_instant.bit           E0041, #2678
//   check_zeroarg_len.bit                  E0050, #3758
//   check_zeroarg_cap.bit                  E0050, #3758
//   check_zeroarg_append.bit               E0050, #3758
//   check_zeroarg_conversion.bit           E0050, #3758
//   check_zeroarg_userconv.bit             E0050, #3758
//   check_trait_method_conflict.bit        E0120, #3369 (was E0103, renumbered #4188)
//   check_trait_method_missing.bit         E0104, #3369
//   check_trait_as_param_type.bit          E0105, #3369
//   check_trait_use_cycle.bit              E0106, #3369
//   check_self_outside_trait.bit           E0040, #3369
//   check_map_ctor_int_arg.bit             E0050, #4065
//   check_map_ctor_string_arg.bit          E0050, #4065
//   check_map_ctor_multi_arg.bit           E0050, #4065
//   check_readonly_field_assign_own_module.bit  E0114, #4066
//   check_readonly_field_assign_foreign.bit     E0114, #4066
//   check_test_decl_outside_test_file.bit       E0115, #4127
//   check_slice_alloc_slice_arg.bit             E0111, #4104
//   check_try_operand_not_fallible.bit          E0116, #4013
//   check_try_operand_not_fallible_control.bit  E0061, #4013
//   check_slice_alloc_bytes_elem.bit            E0111, #4137
//   check_bare_fn_test_shape.test.bit           E0117, #4148
//   check_tuple_literal_type_mismatch.bit       E0041, #4105
//   check_forof_field_unknown.bit               E0123, #4106
//
// REMOVED BY #4105: check_tuple_literal_expr.bit (E0094 x2, #2176). `(a, b)`
// in expression position is a real tuple literal now (SPEC §12.10) instead of
// a parser rejection, so both of that fixture's sites (a parenthesized
// `return` and a `let` initializer) type-check and RUN correctly — see
// _tests_/cases/run_tuple_literal_expr.bit, which replaces it with the accept
// half (the standing rule two paragraphs below: MISSING/acceptance stays with
// the corpus; only a still-rejected diagnostic belongs here). E0094 is
// retired, not reused (diagnostic codes are never renumbered once assigned).
// check_tuple_literal_type_mismatch.bit above pins the diagnostic a
// MALFORMED tuple literal gets instead (E0041, an ordinary element-type
// mismatch on a construct the pinned oracle still cannot parse at all).
//
// REMOVED BY #3779: check_test_signature.bit (E0093 x3, #2080). #3786 dropped
// the `test_` name prefix as `bit test`'s discovery marker for a `.test.bit`
// filename marker (SPEC §19), and E0093 rejected a malformed `test_*`
// signature under exactly that dropped naming rule — a differently-shaped
// function in a `.test.bit` file is now a HELPER, by design, not a rejected
// declaration; there is no longer a naming signal that could tell "meant to
// be a test" apart from "meant to be a helper". compiler/validatetest.bit,
// the rule's only implementation, is deleted; E0093 is retired, not reused
// (diagnostic codes are never renumbered once assigned, spec/SPEC.md's error
// registry). The remaining safety net is E0216 `empty-test-file`
// (compiler/lintapply.bit, spec/LINT.md §4): a `.test.bit` file that
// discovers nothing at all is a lint finding.
//
// WHY THESE LIVE OUTSIDE _tests_/cases/, AND WHY REPINNING CANNOT FIX IT.
//
// scripts/selfhost-diffcheck.sh compares this compiler against the PINNED
// stage0 — the previous RELEASE of this same compiler — over
//     find stdlib examples _tests_/cases _tests_/imports -name '*.bit'
// and classifies "this compiler rejects, the oracle accepts" as FALSEPOS, the
// one outcome it exits 1 on. Every case here asserts a rejection this tree
// introduced, so a golden case under _tests_/cases/ IS the file that turns the
// differential red. Measured with wave 3's four still in the sweep:
// MATCH=661 MISSING=2 FALSEPOS=4 DIFF=4, rc=1, and the four FALSEPOS were
// exactly those four files.
//
// Bumping the stage0 pin does NOT clear them, which is the part worth writing
// down because it is the obvious thing to try. The pin bump to 0.1.8 clears the
// FALSEPOS class whose fixes already SHIPPED — there the oracle is merely stale.
// These fixes are all newer than 0.1.8, so no released compiler emits these
// diagnostics and no available oracle can. Clearing them by repinning would mean
// cutting a release containing this wave and then repinning to it: a full release
// cycle per wave of checker fixes. Do not move these back and reach for the pin.
//
// A known-divergence list is also not the repair: that script refuses one on
// principle (#1883 — "a filter on a differential's ORACLE side can only ever
// hide a difference, never reveal one"), and it deleted the last one.
//
// Same placement, and the same reasoning, as _tests_/bit/constoverflow.bit (#2261)
// and _tests_/bit/genericdiag.bit (#2360/#2243/#2148). The standing rule those
// three settled: a case asserting a diagnostic NO RELEASED COMPILER EMITS goes
// in _tests_/bit/ behind a registered gate; a case asserting ACCEPTANCE — the
// MISSING direction, which does not gate — stays in _tests_/cases/ with the corpus.
// The accept halves of these tickets did stay there (run_error_iface_ok.bit,
// run_comparable_ok.bit). #2236's accept half is _tests_/bit/mainexit.bit instead:
// it was already pinning all four §17.4 `main` forms end to end — exit code,
// stdout and stderr, through `bit run` and through `bit build` — which is a
// stronger statement than a clean `bit check` and needed nothing added.
//
// WHY THIS IS NOT A `contains(err, "error[E0053]")` HARNESS.
//
// constoverflow.bit and genericdiag.bit inline their programs as strings and
// assert with a code plus a needle. That is the right shape when there is no
// `.expected` to begin with. These four arrive WITH one, and golden.bit's own
// header calls the `// error` cases "the only place in the repo that pins
// rendered diagnostic text at all". A needle match is strictly weaker — it
// cannot see a wrong span, a wrong line number, a lost note, a caret of the
// wrong width, or a fifth diagnostic appearing out of nowhere. So the files move
// unchanged, `.expected` and all, and the comparison here is the same byte
// comparison golden.bit performs: `bit check <name>` run with the corpus as its
// working directory, stderr compared whole after the one `--> ./` normalization
// golden.bit applies for the same reason.
//
// NON-VACUITY. This repo has shipped guards that passed over empty input sets,
// so golden.bit's four floors are reproduced rather than assumed:
//
//   1. `BIT_CHECKER_CASES_DIR` and `BIT_BIN` have NO defaults. Unset is a hard
//      failure, never a silent walk of ".".
//   2. The case count is pinned exactly (`expectedCases`). Adding or removing a
//      case must edit it in the same commit. "Fewer than max" is not a floor —
//      zero satisfies it.
//   3. Orphans are detected BOTH ways: every `.bit` needs a readable
//      `.expected` AND every `.expected` needs a `.bit`.
//   4. A wrapper that never reached its `exec` leaves no redirect file, and that
//      is a named failure — never "the compiler errored, as expected". Line 1 of
//      every case must be `// error`, so a `// run` case dropped in here fails
//      loudly instead of being silently judged by the wrong oracle.
//
// It also carries golden.bit's #2084 sweep, because moving these files out of
// _tests_/cases/ would otherwise drop four INVALID programs from it — and invalid
// programs are the only ones that sweep exists for. `--dump-ir` and
// `--dump-ir-pre` bypass the checker, so they are the one path that hands
// lowering a program `bit build` would have refused; they may exit however they
// like, but they must not die by signal.
//
// Usage:
//   BIT_CHECKER_CASES_DIR=$PWD/_tests_/bit/checkercases BIT_BIN=$PWD/bit-out/bin/bit \
//   BIT_STDLIB=$PWD/stdlib bit run _tests_/bit/checkerdiag.bit

import { env, envOr, exit } from "std/os"
import { readFile, writeFile, readDir, exists, remove, mkdir } from "std/fs"
import { hasPrefix, hasSuffix, indexOf, trimSpace, parseInt } from "std/strings"

// THE MANIFEST. Measured on disk (`ls
// _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`, not by incrementing the number seen
// on a stale branch — see the merge-hazard note below). See the header for
// what belongs here and what belongs in _tests_/cases/.
//
// THIS COUNT IS A MERGE HAZARD, and it bit exactly once: #2804 and #2773 each
// added one case and each bumped 20 -> 21 on its own branch. The census COMMENT
// above conflicted (both inserted a line), but this constant did NOT — both
// sides wrote the identical `21`, so git merged it silently while the union on
// disk was 22. Resolve a census conflict by COUNTING THE FILES, never by taking
// either side's number.
// #3762 (post-merge with main) retires check_method_enum_receiver.bit and
// check_method_enum_alias_receiver.bit -- E0095 (enum method receiver
// rejected) is now permanently unreachable, since an enum can never have a
// method in any surviving form -- so 74 (main's count) drops to 72, then
// back up to 73 with check_receiver_form_removed.bit (the new E0103
// rejection fixture #3762's own acceptance requires). Derived from
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`, per this file's own
// merge-hazard rule above: count the files, never take either side's number.
// #3371 (init) then adds 3 (check_init_duplicate, check_init_seal_cross_module,
// check_init_unhandled_fallible), giving 76. Neither branch's own number was
// right at merge time -- main said 73, task-3371-init said 77. Derived with
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #3370 (trait fields) then adds 2 more, giving 78. Its own side said nothing
// here and main said 76; the union on disk is what counts. Derived with
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #4065 (map constructor arity) then adds 3 more (check_map_ctor_int_arg,
// check_map_ctor_string_arg, check_map_ctor_multi_arg), giving 81. Derived
// with `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #4091 (slice-alloc argument TYPE, not just count) then adds 3 more
// (check_slice_alloc_string_arg, check_slice_alloc_bool_arg,
// check_slice_alloc_float_arg), giving 84. Derived with
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #4092 (chan<T>(...) and [N]T(...) construction) then adds 5 more
// (check_chan_ctor_multi_arg, check_chan_ctor_string_arg,
// check_chan_ctor_bool_arg, check_array_ctor_empty,
// check_array_ctor_with_args), giving 89. Derived with
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #4066 (`readonly` class fields) then adds 2 more
// (check_readonly_field_assign_own_module, check_readonly_field_assign_foreign),
// giving 91. Its support module (readonlysupport/stamp.bit, mirroring
// initsealsupport/account.bit's precedent) sits in a subdirectory, invisible
// to this glob — see readonlysupport/stamp.bit's own header. Derived with
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #4127 (the `test` declaration, epic #4126) then adds 1 more
// (check_test_decl_outside_test_file, E0115), giving 92. Derived with
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #4104 (regression guard for the shipped-0.5.0 `[]T(sliceLiteral)`
// address-as-length miscompile) then adds 1 more
// (check_slice_alloc_slice_arg, E0111 — the same code #4091 assigned,
// since the generic argument-type check that code closed already covers a
// slice-typed operand), giving 93. Derived with
// `ls _tests_/bit/checkercases/*.bit | wc -l`.
// #4013 (§18.3, E0116) then adds 2 more — check_try_operand_not_fallible.bit
// (the new diagnostic) and its control, check_try_operand_not_fallible_control.bit
// (proves E0061 still fires alone and is not conjoined with E0116).
// #4137 (regression guard for `isBytesConversion`'s missing elem-byte-sized
// check, the sibling gap #4133's fix did not close — that early return is
